# Frontend has its own build context (frontend/Dockerfile + frontend/.dockerignore).
# The API image (this dir + root Dockerfile COPY . .) needs nothing from it:
# grep of app/ alembic/ scripts/ finds no imports or file reads of frontend/,
# only incidental strings in comments. Excluding the whole tree keeps 600MB+ of
# node_modules / .next / out / coverage / .turbo / test-results out of the
# root build context (was the ~2.5GB pathological API image).
frontend/

# ---- V1-H5A hardening ---------------------------------------------------
# Patterns without **/ only match at the context root; these cover nested
# copies too. tests/test_v1h5a_build_safety.py checks the effective context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.coverage.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.sql
**/*.dump
**/*.backup
**/*.bak
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.claude/
# Generated at runtime (barcodes/QR codes/labels/invoices from local data); the
# Dockerfile recreates the empty directories.
app/static/
# Not used at runtime by the API image.
docs/
frontend-prototype/
# R0b-A e2e harness artefacts: protected evidence, never part of a demo image.
scripts/e2e/
compose.e2e.yml
.gitattributes
# Keep the committed, placeholder-only templates (must stay last).
!.env.*.example
